# starglow

- Label: Star Glow
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 75 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/starglow.html
- Summary (EN): Star Glow adds star-like light streaks to a layer by streaking its bright areas in multiple directions. It finds pixels above a luminance threshold and applies the streaks only to those regions.
- Résumé (FR) : Star Glow ajoute des traînées lumineuses en étoile aux zones claires d'un calque, en les étirant dans plusieurs directions à partir des pixels au-dessus d'un seuil de luminance.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer receiving the effect", "effect (optional): layer controlling which areas get the effect, works with the Threshold parameter", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask whose amount is scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Threshold / Width: luminance level above which pixels glow, and the range on either side", "Streaks: number of streaks spread evenly around 360 degrees", "Streak Length: overall strength of the streaks, negative values trace the opposite direction", "Brightness: lightens and expands the glow at high values, dims and shrinks it at low values", "Streak: Blur (averages samples) or Max (keeps brightest sample, for edge roughness)", "Streak Weight: ramp multiplying pixel values along each streak", "Combine Streaks with: Add, Screen, Hypot, Maximum, or Difference", "Color Mode / Color / Color Ramp / Multiply with Original: tinting of the streaks", "Aberration (Red, Green, Blue): per-channel rotation of streaks for chromatic fringing", "Glimmer, Animate, Pulse Length, Time Scale, Loop Length: shimmer and animation", "Output Star Glow Only: outputs only the glow, usable as a separate AOV or with Blend COP", "Maximum Steps (Advanced): samples taken along each streak"]

- Caveats: ["Long streaks can leave gaps, increase Maximum Steps to fill them", "For a glow or blur in one direction only, use the Glow COP or Streak Blur COP instead"]

